{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":330251,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e780ebcc-4bfa-42ac-bf6d-1d3dd211aaa6","total_cost_usd":1.2046284999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48121,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":27378,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48121,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":27378,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48121},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":30395,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.030475,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":27378,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":48121,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1741534999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"economy-balancer\",\n  \"flight\": {\n    \"dry_mass_kg\": 850,\n    \"fuel_capacity_kg\": 450,\n    \"thrust_n\": 12000,\n    \"fuel_burn_kgs\": 3.2,\n    \"rcs_thrust_n\": 600,\n    \"rcs_fuel_burn_kgs\": 0.16,\n    \"rotation_rate_degs\": 75\n  },\n  \"cargo\": {\n    \"base_slots\": 6,\n    \"compactor_tier\": 1\n  },\n  \"reentry\": {\n    \"heat_capacity\": 100,\n    \"heat_dissipation_s\": 5,\n    \"cargo_damage_interval_s\": 3,\n    \"unstaged_heat_multiplier\": 3.0,\n    \"off_retrograde_penalty\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"ablation\": {\n    \"cycle_toll_base_pct\": 0.53,\n    \"cycle_toll_growth\": 1.9,\n    \"heat_cost_coefficient\": 0.00029,\n    \"heat_cost_exponent\": 2.4,\n    \"skim_peak\": 26,\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier\": [1.0, 0.94, 0.9, 0.88],\n    \"heat_index\": { \"suborbital\": 73, \"low\": 100, \"high\": 138 },\n    \"cost_curve\": {\n      \"suborbital\": [9.13, 9.67, 11.57, 15.58],\n      \"low\": [18.83, 18.03, 19.1, 22.71],\n      \"high\": [40.16, 36.43, 35.67, 38.41]\n    },\n    \"plate_capacity_pct\": 100,\n    \"optimal_skims\": { \"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2 }\n  },\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"soft_landing_ms\": 5.0,\n    \"damage_per_ms_over\": 6.0,\n    \"no_gear_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"fragile_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"parachute_drag_coefficient\": 1.8,\n    \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms\": 4.6\n  },\n  \"tow_fee\": {\n    \"free_radius_m\": 2000,\n    \"max_fee_fraction\": 0.5,\n    \"curve\": \"linear\"\n  },\n  \"eva\": {\n    \"suit_mass_kg\": 120,\n    \"jetpack_thrust_n\": 500,\n    \"jetpack_fuel_kg\": 24,\n    \"jetpack_burn_kgs\": 0.7,\n    \"base_tether_slots\": 2,\n    \"magnet_hold_force_n\": 900,\n    \"magnet_range_screens\": 0.125,\n    \"latch_jerk_coefficient\": 0.5,\n    \"swing_jerk_coefficient\": 0.6\n  },\n  \"economy\": {\n    \"launch_cost\": 100,\n    \"replate_cost_per_pct\": 3,\n    \"repair_cost_per_pct\": 5,\n    \"band_value_multiplier\": { \"suborbital\": 1.0, \"low\": 2.4, \"high\": 5.5 },\n    \"size_class_base_value\": { \"small\": 40, \"medium\": 90, \"oversized\": 320 },\n    \"fragile_value_premium\": 3.0\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 400, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 620 },\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1200, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 850 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 350, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 15000 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1000, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 19000 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 500, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 9 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1500, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 12 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 450, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 130 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1300, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 165 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 420, \"effect\": \"parachute_drag_coefficient\", \"value\": 2.6 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1200, \"effect\": \"parachute_drag_coefficient\", \"value\": 3.6 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 380, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 1400 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1100, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 2100 }\n  ],\n  \"balance_notes\": [\n    \"Full-hold mass doubling (GDD 2.3.5) is arithmetic, not aspiration. Spawn-weighting the eight hand-tetherable suborbital pieces gives 15855/86 = 184.4 kg and 118/86 = 1.372 crushed slots per piece, i.e. 134.4 kg per slot. Six base slots is 806 kg against dry_mass_kg = 850, so a full starting hold is 1.95x the ship's dry mass. A medium-heavy hold (three spent booster rings, 1380 kg) reads 2.6x and a filler hold of insulation wads reads 0.42x, so 'roughly doubles' is the centre of the distribution rather than a best case.\",\n    \"dry_mass_kg = 850 is the POST-STAGING reentry mass (hull, shield, hold). The schema has no field for the jettisoned stage's structural mass, so I could not put it where it belongs; the ascent arithmetic below assumes it is ~15% of fuel_capacity, i.e. 68 kg. That is the one number in the flight block a reader cannot check against this file, and it should be added to the schema rather than folded into dry_mass_kg by the Coder.\",\n    \"Flight budget. Exhaust velocity is thrust_n / fuel_burn_kgs = 12000 / 3.2 = 3750 m/s (Isp 382 s). Liftoff mass 850 + 68 + 450 = 1368 kg, burnout 918 kg, so total Delta-v = 3750 * ln(1368/918) = 3750 * 0.3987 = 1495 m/s. Circularising in the suborbital band costs the Researcher's 842 m/s plus roughly 300 m/s of gravity and drag loss, about 1150 m/s. Deorbit is nearly free by vis-viva: dropping periapsis to r_p = 290 km from r = 352.5 km gives v_apo = sqrt(2.5e11*(2/352500 - 1/321250)) = 800 m/s, so the burn is 842 - 800 = 42 m/s. The ~300 m/s remainder is skim-shaping margin, which is exactly the resource the ablation model spends. Liftoff TWR = 12000 / (1368 * 4.0) = 2.19.\",\n    \"heat_index is derived, not chosen. Peak convective flux scales as v^3 (Sutton-Graves, exponent 3.04) and as sqrt(beta) for a ballistic entry. The Researcher's entry-interface speeds are 864 / 906 / 954 m/s, giving velocity ratios (864/906)^3 = 0.867 and (954/906)^3 = 1.168 against the low band. Full-hold staged masses from the catalog's mass-per-crushed-slot figures (134.4 / 247.6 / 403.9 kg per slot at 6 slots) are 1656 / 2336 / 3273 kg, so beta ratios are 0.708 and 1.400 and sqrt(beta) ratios are 0.841 and 1.183. Product: 0.729 / 1.000 / 1.381, normalised to heat_index 73 / 100 / 138. This is the beta lever the Researcher pointed at when he warned that entry speed alone only spreads the bands 1.35x; the catalog's mass gradient supplies the rest.\",\n    \"Ablation optimum. Evaluating cost(band,k) = 0.53 * sum(1.9^i, i=0..k) + 0.00029 * (heat_index * skim_heat_multiplier[k])^2.4 + k * 0.00029 * 26^2.4 gives suborbital [9.13, 9.67, 11.57, 15.58] (min at 0), low [18.83, 18.03, 19.10, 22.71] (min at 1) and high [40.16, 36.43, 35.67, 38.41] (min at 2). The skim heat unit is 0.00029 * 2488.5 = 0.722 %/skim and the thermal-fatigue tolls are 0.53, 1.01, 1.92 and 3.65% on cycles 0-3. Growth 1.9 is what closes the optimum: the heat saving from skim 3 at the high band is only 0.00029 * (106133 - 100562) = 1.62%, and the fourth cycle's toll of 3.65% alone outprices it. A flat toll cannot do this, because the saving series and the toll series would both be affine in k.\",\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier is a guess, and I have marked it as one. I run before the flight simulator, so [1.0, 0.94, 0.90, 0.88] is a conservative reading of the charter's guidance rather than a measurement. It is also a single global array while the physics says the effect is larger from lower bands, which pushes the optimum DOWN at low altitude - the opposite of what the design wants - so the band ordering here is carried by heat_index and by the convexity of the 2.4 exponent, not by the skim curve. If the Playtester returns measured values I expect heat_cost_coefficient and cycle_toll_growth to need retuning together; changing the multipliers alone will move all three optima.\",\n    \"Parachute at full hold. Terminal speed is sqrt(2mg / (rho * Cd * A)), which is the square-root-of-mass growth GDD 2.3.2 asks for. At rho0 = 1.0 kg/m^3 and g = 4.0, Cd = 1.8 over a 348 m^2 canopy gives rho*Cd*A = 626 and a full suborbital hold (850 + 806 = 1656 kg) lands at sqrt(13248/626) = 4.60 m/s - under the 5 m/s line, but only just. Empty (850 kg) it is 3.30 m/s. That canopy area is the second number this schema cannot hold; it pairs with parachute_drag_coefficient and the Coder needs both.\",\n    \"Storage and Parachute are a forced pair, by construction. A full LOW-band hold is 850 + 1486 = 2336 kg and lands at 4.60 * sqrt(2336/1656) = 5.46 m/s - a hard landing, and double damage on the fragile half of that band's value. Parachute tier 1 (Cd 2.6) brings it to 4.54 m/s; a full high-band hold (3273 kg) reads 6.47 m/s and needs tier 2 (Cd 3.6) to reach 4.57 m/s. Each band therefore buys exactly one parachute tier, and each Storage tier pushes the ship back over the line, which is GDD 2.3.6's double-edged claim made literal.\",\n    \"Lazy run breaks even with room. A suborbital run at optimum burns 9.13% of plate, so replating costs 9.13 * 3 = 27, and launch_cost = 100 is 2.5 cheap smalls at size_class_base_value.small = 40 (GDD 2.3.6's '2-3 pieces of cheap junk'). Total fixed cost 127. Six crushed slots of the cheapest thing in the band is 6 * 40 = 240, so even the laziest full hold clears 113. The spawn-weighted expected haul is 45.0 per slot (5310/86 = 61.7 per piece over 1.372 slots), i.e. 270 gross and 143 net. The low band at 2.4x runs 123 per slot, 738 gross and 584 net after a 18.03% descent, so band progression is roughly a 4x jump in run value.\",\n    \"No shear under steady tow, proved rather than tuned. Steady-state tension in cable i is T_i = m_i * a = m_i * F / (m_suit + sum of towed mass). Because m_i is one term of that denominator sum and m_suit > 0, T_i < F for every legal load - the tension can approach jetpack_thrust_n = 500 N but can never reach it, no matter how heavy the piece or how many slots are filled. The worst case in the catalog is a lone iridium_battery_stack at 1150 kg: 1150 * 500 / (120 + 1150) = 453 N. magnet_hold_force_n = 900 sits 1.8x above the asymptote, so shear can only ever fire on the impulsive terms. Latch shear at coefficient 0.5 trips at v_closing = 900 / (0.5 * m): 12.9 m/s for a 140 kg hull panel, 4.7 m/s for a 380 kg truss, 2.6 m/s for a 700 kg bus frame - heavier pieces sit closer to the limit at every tier, as GDD 2.3.4 requires.\",\n    \"Tow fee. free_radius_m = 2000 is the pad zone; beyond it the fee is 0.5 * (d - 2000) / (785398 - 2000), where 785398 m is half of 2*pi*250000. It is zero at the pad edge, exactly 0.5 at the antipode, clamped to [0, 0.5] so it can never go negative and never exceed half the haul, and it is charged against haul value only, so it cannot touch savings (GDD 2.3.3).\",\n    \"heat_capacity = 100 is a gate, not a decoration. Because heat_index is normalised to a full-hold direct entry, a full low-band hold flown straight in peaks at exactly 100 and starts damaging cargo; one skim drops it to 94 and it survives. A full high-band hold peaks at 138 and cannot be flown direct at any tier - two skims bring it to 124, which still needs heat_shield tier 1 (capacity 130). That is why the heat_shield upgrades raise capacity rather than reduce ablation: GDD 2.3.1 says shield upgrades buy margin, not immunity, and ablation here is quoted as a percentage of plate so capacity cannot change it.\",\n    \"Staging stays one-way. No parameter in this file restores thrust after jettison: thrust_n, rcs_thrust_n and both burn rates belong to the stage that leaves. The only post-stage impulse is eva.jetpack_thrust_n = 500 N applied to the hull, which at a staged 1656 kg gives 0.30 m/s^2 and, across the full 24 kg of EVA propellant, about 7 m/s of orbit change - a rescue, not an engine, exactly as GDD 2.3.1 scopes it.\",\n    \"EVA handling. Empty astronaut acceleration is 500 / 120 = 4.17 m/s^2. Two spawn-weighted suborbital pieces (368 kg towed) gives 500 / 488 = 1.02 m/s^2, a 4x drop the player feels immediately; two low-band mediums (bus frame plus tank shell, 1320 kg) gives 500 / 1440 = 0.35 m/s^2. jetpack_fuel_kg = 24 at 0.7 kg/s is 34 s of continuous burn, which is 143 m/s of Delta-v clean and 11.7 m/s with two low-band mediums in tow - enough for one loaded round trip of a few hundred metres and not two, which is the trips-versus-control decision GDD 2.3.4 wants.\"\n  ],\n  \"catalog_concerns\": [\n    \"satellite_bus_frame (and the low band's mediums generally), mass_kg: at 700 kg against any plausible suit mass, a two-tether load of low-band mediums leaves the astronaut at 0.35 m/s^2 - about 37 s to cross 200 m and stop. I balanced against it rather than around it, but if playtesting reads that as unresponsive rather than heavy, the fix is in the catalog's mass column, not in jetpack_thrust_n: raising thrust enough to fix the loaded case makes the empty astronaut twitchy.\",\n    \"iridium_battery_stack, mass_kg: 1150 kg is the heaviest hand-tetherable piece authored, and it sets the ceiling for magnet_hold_force_n via the latch-jerk term - a gentle latch on it shears above 1.6 m/s closing speed at base tier. It is a high-band piece and therefore deferred, but it is the number that will decide hand_magnet tier 3 if the high band ships.\",\n    \"cracked_solar_array and parabolic_dish_section, size_class plus fragile: a fragile medium is uncrushable and so costs 4 of the 6 base slots. Two of them fill a starting hold with two pieces, which makes the fragile detour an all-or-nothing decision in the low band rather than the 'sometimes worth it' the GDD asks for. The honest fix is base_slots, which the GDD's own walkthrough puts on screen at 6, so I left it at 6 and priced around it.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":260615,"ttft_stream_ms":1858,"time_to_request_ms":213,"type":"result","duration_ms":328671,"uuid":"02b2603e-3655-4215-9e48-4fd873e251a9"}
